  "summary_en": "Mauritius' 2018 national AI strategy prepared by a government working group. It prioritises AI adoption in manufacturing, healthcare, fintech, agriculture, ocean economy and transport, and proposes an AI Council, incentives, skills development, and a regulatory, ethics and data protection framework. Robotics appear only incidentally.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Establish a Mauritius Artificial Intelligence Council (MAIC) to oversee projects and impact.",
   "Provide matching grants, tax credits and training incentives, plus the existing Regulatory Sandbox Licence.",
   "Set up a permanent ethics committee and a working group to amend data protection legislation.",
   "Humans must be able to override AI decisions; market players should define liability parameters.",
   "Expedite the IP Bill and leave IP with private developers."
